  "published": "2026-10-26T15:46:24Z",
  "modified": "2026-10-26T15:46:24Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak in the YUV decoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-61868.patch: relinquish the scanline buffer\n       and destroy the chroma image when OpenBlob() fails in ReadYUVImage()\n       in coders/yuv.c\n     - CVE-2026-61868\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak in the MIFF encoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-61869.patch: destroy the quantum info before\n       throwing on compress_pixels and colormap allocation failures in\n       WriteMIFFImage() in coders/miff.c\n     - CVE-2026-61869\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: infinite loop when reading bzip2-compressed data\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106565.patch: set eof on a short read with\n       BZ_OK in ReadBlob() and do not clear eof in EOFBlob() in\n       magick/blob.c\n     - CVE-2026-106565\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: infinite loop in the PSD decoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106567.patch: reject non-positive and\n       overflowing resource block offsets in ParseImageResourceBlocks() in\n       coders/psd.c\n     - CVE-2026-106567\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: coder security policy bypass\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106579.patch: check the coder policy against\n       the resolved coder name instead of the requested magick string in\n       ReadImage() and WriteImage() in magick/constitute.c\n     - CVE-2026-106579",
